 have good comprehension  and this of course is my goal in my  90-day challenge with arabic if i can  understand podcasts in arabic even if i  can't use all the words then i can turn  them on in the morning i'm listening to  a new podcast i'm understanding 80 of it  it's all washing over my brain  and in time as i gain more familiarity  with the language i will start to  activate some of those words but my  active vocabulary what i can use will  always be a smaller subset of the words  that i understand but in terms of  progressing in the language what's key  is comprehension and even if i have now  as i'm having conversations with my  arabic tutors i don't worry about what i  can't do by the way this is a t-shirt i  got we my old-timers hockey team played  against an old-timer's hockey team from  japan and they brought us this these  nice t-shirts  looks like the car the character for a  well like e in japanese or  you know  jing in chinese anyway as i was saying  so  uh when i speak with my tutors  it doesn't bother me when i fall down  i want to focus on understanding them  and all of that is helping my brain to  get used to the language and as i  struggle to find words  and then afterwards i remember the words  that i struggled to find i become more  attentive to those words when i see them  again in some context so  the i see these conversations as again  promoting better comprehension promoting  more attentiveness attentiveness to the  language  it's not where i want to perform and oh  i did well or i didn't do well because  inevitably  i'm going to do better sometimes than at  other times and i will gradually get  better at speaking but it won't be a  straight line  i might do well for a while and then i  might stumble it might be  my the vibes that this tutor gives me or  or whatever it might be a poor  connection on skype so the main thing  for me  is comprehension  and what that does to me is is it  reduces the level of of uh  apprehensiveness tension i'm 